h":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.03837097853409769,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":36.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.3614,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"American Integrity Insurance Group, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates as an insurance company in the United States. The company offers personal residential property insurance for single-family homeowners and condominium owners, as well as coverage for vacant dwellings and investment properties. It also provides manufactured home, commercial residential, dwelling property, and specialty insurance products. In addition, the company offers optional endorsements that provide higher levels of standard coverage and optional coverage, such as personal injury, animal liability, identity recovery, and golf cart physical; and flood insurance products. It distributes its products through the Voluntary Market, which includes partnerships with independent agents, national and regional insurance companies, homebuilder-affiliated agents, and direct-to-consumer channels. American Integrity Insurance Group, Inc. was incorporated in 2006 and is headquartered in Tampa, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Robert Craig Ritchie | Founder, CEO & Director | Age 66 | Compensation: $3.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 313 people. Revenue per employee of $883K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $425K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $34K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["American Integrity Insurance Gr is a small-cap financial services business with a $528M market cap on $276M of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 86% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 77-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $133M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 48 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.39\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 36% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $15.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 12% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 74% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 79% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Stay Ahead of the Game With American Integrity Insurance (AII) Q3 Earnings: Wall Street's Insights on Key Metrics","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024055/stay-ahead-of-the-game-with-american-integrity-insurance-aii-q3-earnings-wall-street-s-insights-on-key-metrics?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cnfm_preview-3024055","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793884512.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Robert C. Ritchie to Sell 75,000 Shares of American Integrity Insurance Group Stock","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/robert-c-ritchie-to-sell-75000-shares-of-american-integrity-insurance-group-stock","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793820784.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.586,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"American Integrity Insurance Group, Inc. Announces Third Quarter 2026 Earnings Release Date and Conference Call","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/american-integrity-insurance-group-inc-201500880.html","date":"2026-10-27","timestamp":1793132100.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":